From: ane-stack
Subject: [PATCH 0005] milc: accept a compiled .mlmodelc in `milc run`

Stacking: apply after 0001, 0002, 0003, 0004 (this diff is generated against
that base; its context includes 0004's shard-dispatch fix).

Before this patch `milc run <arg>` accepted only a `.mlpackage`: it read the
protobuf spec from `Data/com.apple.CoreML/model.mlmodel`, compiled the package
if needed, then ran. A precompiled `.mlmodelc` failed immediately with

  model.mlmodel: No such file or directory

because a compiled artifact carries the spec as MIL text (`model.mil`), not the
protobuf. cmd_run now detects a `.mlmodelc` (presence of `model.mil`) and, for
that path, parses the `func main(...)` signature to recover the input/state
features the run loop needs (name, shape, dtype, is_state), then loads and runs
the artifact as-is with no recompile.

Dtypes map to the CoreML protobuf codes `dtype_of` already understands, so feed
synthesis works unchanged. Adds a CLI integration test that builds a stateful
model, compiles it, and asserts `milc run <mlmodelc>` succeeds.

Verified: `milc run /tmp/ir_fixed.compiled/ir_fixed.mlmodelc --units ane`
runs 3 steps on cpu+ane (median 56.42us). Package path unaffected.

